Rule 1 (channel_shuffle input tensor must have more than 2 dimensions and groups must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) > 2 ∧ v_2 > 0
>>
Rule 2 (groups must be a factor of the number of channels in the input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_1, 1) / v_2 * v_2
>>
Rule 3 (groups must be less than or equal to the number of channels in the input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 4 (if the number of channels is 0, then groups must be 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if shape(v_1, 1) = 0 then v_2 = 1
>>
Rule 5 (if groups is greater than 1, the number of channels must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 > 1 then shape(v_1, 1) > 0
>>
Rule 6 (the number of channels should be divisible by groups)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1)] : shape(v_1, 1) = v_2 * i
>>
Rule 7 (If the input is exactly 3D, then the shuffle can proceed. Otherwise it needs to be >3D)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 then true else ndim(v_1) > 3
>>
Rule 8 (groups is 1 if and only if the number of channels is arbitrary )
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= (v_2 = 1) = (ndim(v_1) > 0)
>>
Rule 9 (groups has to be smaller or equal than channel size and greater than 0 if channel size is greater than 0)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= (shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ v_2 > 0 ∧ v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, 1)) ∨ (shape(v_1, 1) = 0 ∧ v_2 > 0)
>>
Rule 10 (channels size is smaller than 10 or groups is not equal to 5)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= shape(v_1, 1) < 10 ∨ v_2 ≠ 5
>>
Rule 11 (if channels is greater than 1 then groups must be an integer.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: float ⊎ int} |= if shape(v_1, 1) > 1 then (v_2 - (v_2 / 1) = 0)
>>
Rule 12 (if groups is not 1, the input tensor must have a channel dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 ≠ 1 then ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 13 (The product of groups and a constant has to be equal to channel size)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3: int} |= shape(v_1, 1) = v_2 * v_3
>>
Rule 14 (If groups is equal to channel then the only change is possible in last two dimenstions.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 = shape(v_1, 1) then (ndim(v_1) = 4)
>>
Rule 15 (The number of channels must be greater than 1 if groups is greater than 1 or else output is same as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 > 1 then shape(v_1, 1) > 1
>>
Rule 16 (For 3D tensor number of channels should be greater than groups.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 3) then (shape(v_1, 1) > v_2)
>>
Rule 17 (For any n-d tensor if groups is equal to 1 then (n-1) dimensions should be positive.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 = 1 then (∀i ∈ [1, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0)
>>
Rule 18 (Shape of input must be 4D and channel size must be exactly divisible by group size for the output to have integer shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ (shape(v_1, 1) / v_2) = (shape(v_1, 1) / v_2 * 1)
